This goal model provides a hierarchical decomposition of the multi‐robot resource collection and delivery mission. The use of sequential (";") operators in the collection and delivery phases ensures that each step is executed in order, while the parallel ("#") operator in the multi‐robot coordination goal allows for concurrent execution of assignment and coordination tasks. The fallback (not explicitly used here) could be incorporated if additional conditional branches were needed; however, the current design uses sequential execution with conditional (query) checks to trigger specific tasks.

